# Montr Secure — Docker build-context ignore (canonical source).
#
# The compose build context is the REPO ROOT (`context: ../..`). Docker/BuildKit
# selects the ignore file that matches the Dockerfile being built:
#   1. deploy/docker/Dockerfile.<svc>.dockerignore  (per-service, this file's
#      siblings — kept byte-identical to this canonical copy), else
#   2. the repo-root .dockerignore                   (fallback).
# These deploy-scoped files are a SUPERSET of the repo-root .dockerignore, so a
# build never regresses to a fat context. All patterns are relative to the
# context root (the repo root).

# --- Dependencies & build output (reinstalled/recompiled inside the image) ---
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Test & coverage artifacts (prod images never ship tests) ---
**/coverage
**/.vitest
tests

# --- VCS / CI / editor / git hooks ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea

# --- Secrets & local env — NEVER copy into an image (golden rule #1) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets

# --- Docs, corpus, sample repos, sibling deploy trees (not needed to compile) ---
docs
corpus
packages/fixtures/sample-repos
deploy/helm
deploy/airgap

# Markdown: drop everything except the repo-root README.
**/*.md
!README.md

# --- OS / logs / scratch ---
.DS_Store
**/*.log
tmp
.cache
